# local-llamacpp-3050oem-4b-q4_0 — authoritative configuration.
#
# The directory name is documentation; this file decides. Never copy a slot value
# out of the directory name into a CLI flag (NAMING.md, "The name is a claim").
#
# Committed on purpose and deliberately NOT gitignored. A real environment
# variable always wins over it: Makefiles use ?= and dotenv does not overwrite.
#
# FORKED 2026-10-13 from local-llamacpp-3050oem-2b-q4_0, its E2B sister on the same
# card, host and llama.cpp binary. Slot 4 is the only slot that differs. Values
# marked "2B" were measured on the E2B rig and carried; re-measured ones say so.

# ── Model ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Exact Q4_0 rebuild of Google's E4B QAT GGUF: every weight matrix Q4_0, from
# google/gemma-4-E4B-it-qat-q4_0-unquantized on the trained grid step (built in
# local-llamacpp-1650ti-4b-q4_0/benchmarks/runs/2026-09-30-exact-gguf-e4b-1650ti).
# Downloaded here 2026-10-13 from revision 8b7c081e; sha256sum matched.
MODEL_NAME=xbill9/gemma-4-E4B-it-qat-q4_0-exact-gguf
MODEL_PATH=/home/xbill/models/gemma-4-E4B-it-qat-q4_0-exact/gemma-4-E4B-it-q4_0-exact.gguf
MODEL_SHA256=5462cc102b7d22c4748f9b8e82091f2ae064e10a45525151af6f9a7d0da7caf9

# Slot 5 of the directory name. Every weight matrix in the file is Q4_0.
QUANTIZATION=q4_0

# ── Hardware ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MEASURED-STATIC 2026-10-13, `nvidia-smi --query-gpu=name,compute_cap,memory.total,
# memory.free,driver_version,pci.device_id`: PCI 10de:2508, GA106. Ampere, sm_86,
# with tensor cores (the parent's TU117 has none). Host: ASUS X99-A, i7-5820K
# (6C/12T Haswell-E, AVX2, no AVX-512), 46 GiB RAM, hostname `gpu`.
ACCELERATOR_TYPE="NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3050 OEM"
COMPUTE_CAPABILITY=8.6
VRAM_TOTAL_MIB=8192
VRAM_FREE_MIB=7875
NVIDIA_DRIVER=615.78.08
CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0
TENSOR_PARALLEL_SIZE=1

# ── Runtime ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Cloned fresh 2026-10-13 and built with `make build`: GGML_CUDA=ON, CUDA_ARCH=86,
# GGML_NATIVE=ON, Release, FORCE_MMQ off. gcc 16.2.0, CUDA 13.4 (V13.4.92) at
# /usr/local/cuda, which is NOT on PATH by default on this host.
LLAMA_CPP_DIR=/home/xbill/llama.cpp
LLAMA_CPP_COMMIT=77c4540ce
LLAMA_SERVER_BIN=/home/xbill/llama.cpp/build/bin/llama-server

# ── Serving ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The endpoint is not discovered. It is known before the process starts, which
# is the one place CLAUDE.md's "never hardcode an endpoint" rule does not apply
# — there is no QR -> node -> external IP chain here to walk.
#
# HOST=0.0.0.0 since 2026-10-13: listen on every interface so the LAN can reach
# it (eno1 is 192.168.0.156). No auth and no firewall on this host, so anyone on
# the LAN can use it. ENDPOINT stays on loopback: it is what the Makefile, the
# MCP server and sweep.py call, and 127.0.0.1 reaches a 0.0.0.0 listener.
HOST=0.0.0.0
PORT=8080
ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:8080

# N_GPU_LAYERS=99 offloads every block. `make info`: 2.43 GiB of weights must be
# resident; per_layer_token_embd (1.585 GB, 38% of the file) is TENSOR_READ_LAZY by
# default and OVERRIDE_TENSORS below moves it onto the card. MEASURED 2026-10-13
# (benchmarks/runs/2026-10-13-first-light-3050oem) at -c 131072: 4938 MiB with the
# table on the host, 6430 on the card, 6662 with the drafter. Never pass --no-mmap.
N_GPU_LAYERS=99

# The trained maximum (n_ctx_train 131072), for one user. KV at this size is
# 2048 + 40 MiB, against E2B's 768 + 12. MEASURED 2026-10-13 (llama-bench by depth,
# first-light run): generation 60 / 56 / 47 / 39 / 30 tok/s with 0 / 8k / 32k /
# 65k / 120k tokens already in context. With --parallel N each slot gets
# CONTEXT_SIZE / N.
CONTEXT_SIZE=131072

# f16. 2B: q8_0 K+V was 0.961x prefill and 0.926x decode. Not re-measured on E4B.
KV_CACHE_TYPE=f16

# 2B: 1.133x prefill, 1.071x decode against -fa 0. Not re-measured on E4B.
FLASH_ATTENTION=1

# Prometheus metrics at $ENDPOINT/metrics (llama-server answers 501 without
# --metrics). For operational questions and for checking the prompt cache was
# defeated in a sweep, never for the benchmark decode column: --decode-source
# auto must keep resolving to `stream` (CLAUDE.md).
METRICS=1

# 2B: -t 4 within 0.5% of -t 6; decode runs on the card. Not re-measured on E4B.
THREADS=6
# Carried from the parent; UNMEASURED here. Prefill runs on the card.
THREADS_BATCH=12

# 1: this rig's normal use is one interactive session. Concurrency UNMEASURED on
# E4B. llama.cpp SPLITS --ctx-size ACROSS SLOTS.
PARALLEL_SLOTS=1

# Thinking, server-wide: llama-server --reasoning {on,off,auto}. OFF so answers
# arrive directly in `content`. A request can still ask for it with
# "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": true}, which is what sweep.py does.
REASONING=off

# llama.cpp's default. UNMEASURED on this card; the parent measured it marginally
# worse on the 1650 Ti, which has no tensor cores. This card does.
GGML_CUDA_FORCE_MMQ=OFF

# per_layer_token_embd ON THE CARD, passed as -ot. MEASURED 2026-10-13 (first-light
# run, llama-bench r=5, ABBA): prefill 1.023x at pp512 and 1.014x at pp2048, decode
# 1.000x, for 1492 MiB (4938 -> 6430 MiB at -c 131072). Smaller gain than E2B's
# 1.036x / 1.024x. Empty this to keep the table in the mmap and save the memory.
OVERRIDE_TENSORS=per_layer_token_embd\.weight=CUDA0

# ── Speculative decoding ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Google's drafter for this checkpoint, google/gemma-4-E4B-it-qat-q4_0-unquantized-
# assistant (revision 27f8d204, 4 layers sharing the target's KV), ships as bf16 on
# its 4-bit QAT grid. SINCE 2026-10-14 this rig serves it as exact Q4_0 on that grid
# (59 MB), published at SPEC_DRAFT_HF and fetched by `make draft`; SHA-256 below.
# MEASURED 2026-10-14 (local-llamacpp-3050oem-2b-q4_0/benchmarks/runs/2026-10-14-drafter-q4exact-3050oem):
# against the Q8_0 conversion it replaces, 100.0 against 100.4 tok/s at 2 drafted tokens,
# same acceptance, GSM8K and BFCL level, 4499 against 4537 MiB VRAM. Passed as -md with
# --spec-type draft-mtp. The numbers below came from the Q8_0 drafter.
# MEASURED 2026-10-13 (benchmarks/runs/2026-10-13-spec-mtp-3050oem): drafting 2
# tokens per step is best, 1.72x decode overall greedy (1.54x story .. 2.21x code)
# and 1.70x sampled at temperature 0.8; 3 tokens is level (1.71x) and best on code,
# 4 is worse. Costs 232 MiB VRAM and 3.3% of prompt speed. Greedy output at 2 and 3
# drafted tokens is byte-identical to serving without it (18 of 18, ~25-token prompts); at 4 it
# differs. With 2k+ tokens of prompt it differs too (2026-10-14-drafter-divergence-3050oem).
# Empty SPEC_DRAFT_MODEL to turn off.
SPEC_DRAFT_MODEL=/home/xbill/models/gemma-4-E4B-it-qat-assistant/gemma-4-E4B-it-qat-assistant-q4_0-exact.gguf
SPEC_DRAFT_SHA256=dc965cb963e56b86fbc04db8efec83163886085e88514574650a57fa55a2ee24
SPEC_DRAFT_HF=xbill9/gemma-4-E4B-it-qat-assistant-q4_0-exact-gguf
SPEC_DRAFT_HF_REVISION=a9468097e5feb9df13d25bd624f47edabfda0992
SPEC_DRAFT_N_MAX=2
